a_valid": true, "result_ok": false, "error_code": "POINT_NOT_FOUND", "error_msg": "point TI-201 not found", "result_data": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 1.3719999997192645, "intended_entities": ["histories.TI-201"], "referenced_entities": ["points.TI-201"]}, {"turn": 3, "state": "CONFIG_HISTORY", "visible_tools": [{"name": "manage_history", "allowed_actions": ["enable_history", "list_history", "set_retention"]}, {"name": "manage_points", "allowed_actions": ["list_points"]}], "visible_count": 2, "selected": "manage_history", "action": "enable_history", "args": {"action": "enable_history", "tag": "PI-201", "storage_mode": "periodic", "sample_interval_s": "1.0", "retention_days": "30"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": false, "error_code": "POINT_NOT_FOUND", "error_msg": "point PI-201 not found", "result_data": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 1.053999999385269, "intended_entities": ["histories.PI-201"], "referenced_entities": ["points.PI-201"]}, {"turn": 3, "state": "CONFIG_HISTORY", "visible_tools": [{"name": "manage_history", "allowed_actions": ["enable_history", "list_history", "set_retention"]}, {"name": "manage_points", "allowed_actions": ["list_points"]}], "visible_count": 2, "selected": "manage_history", "action": "enable_history", "args": {"action": "enable_history", "tag": "FI-201", "storage_mode": "periodic", "sample_interval_s": "1.0", "retention_days": "30"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": false, "error_code": "POINT_NOT_FOUND", "error_msg": "point FI-201 not found", "result_data": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 1.0529999999562278, "intended_entities": ["histories.FI-201"], "referenced_entities": ["points.FI-201"]}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:43d4f3e3424d08e6d0df74e774e92c960d43209e2c18f450ef8c3b2b7ba60734", "final_hash": "sha256:43d4f3e3424d08e6d0df74e774e92c960d43209e2c18f450ef8c3b2b7ba60734", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 989, "output_tokens": 396, "latency_ms": 8513.79420000012, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "当前阶段下，我的工具只能查询点位和历史配置，还**不支持创建新点位**。\n\n需要切换到 **CONFIG_POINT** 阶段才能为您添加这三个 AI 点位并配置历史记录。\n\n您的需求我已记录：\n| 点位名称 | 类型 | 历史记录 |\n|---------|------|---------|\n| TI-201 | AI (模拟量输入) | ✅ 启用 |\n| PI-201 | AI (模拟量输入) | ✅ 启用 |\n| FI-201 | AI (模拟量输入) | ✅ 启用 |\n\n正在切换到配置阶段...\n\nnext_state: CONFIG_POINT", "reasoning": "The user wants to add three IO points: TI-201, PI-201, FI-201, all are AI (Analog Input) type, with history enabled.\n\nHowever, looking at my current available tools:\n1. `manage_history` - only has `list_history` action\n2. `manage_points` - only has `list_points` action\n\nNeither of these tools currently supports creating points. I can only:\n- List history configurations\n- List existing points\n\nI cannot create new points with the current tool set. According to my behavior guidelines:\n- \"若当前阶段的可用工具不满足需求，你可以在回复的纯文本中包含 \"next_state: 阶段名\" 来切换到【可切换的下一阶段】中的合适阶段\"\n\nThe available next stages are: ASK_USER, BIND_POINTS, CONFIG_ALARM, CONFIG_HISTORY, CONFIG_POINT, CONFIG_SCRIPT, DEPLOY, DONE, GENERATE_LAYOUT, MANAGE_PAGES, VALIDATE\n\nTo create/configure points, I should switch to `CONFIG_POINT` stage which would likely have the create_points action available.\n\nLet me inform the user about the situation and switch to the appropriate stage."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1400, "output_tokens": 435, "latency_ms": 9566.294000000198, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的，让我先查看一下当前已有的点位配置情况。", "reasoning": "The user has confirmed I'm now in the CONFIG_POINT stage. Let me check what tools are available now. However, looking at the system prompt, it says the current available tools are:\n- manage_history: only list_history action\n- manage_points: only list_points action\n\nIt seems the tools haven't changed. Let me try to use manage_points to list current points first to understand the current state, and see if perhaps I should try to call a create action even though it's not listed.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the system prompt, it says \"当前允许 actions: list_points\" for manage_points. This means I still can only list points, not create them.\n\nWait, the user is saying I've entered CONFIG_POINT stage. Perhaps the tools have been updated but not reflected in the initial prompt. Let me try to call manage_points with a create action to see what happens.\n\nActually, I should follow the rules strictly - the available actions listed are only \"list_points\" for manage_points. I cannot invent a \"create_points\" action.\n\nBut the user is telling me to continue with the task. Let me first list the existing points to check current status, and then see if I need to report that the create action is not available in this stage either.\n\nActually, let me re-read the instructions more carefully. It says \"当前允许 actions\" - this might mean these are the currently allowed actions in the CONFIG_POINT stage. If create_points is not listed, I truly cannot use it.\n\nLet me try listing the points first to understand the current state, and then I'll need to inform the user if I cannot create points with the available tools.\n\nHmm, but the user explicitly told me to enter this stage to complete the task. Let me try calling manage_points and see what happens. Maybe the tool definition has more actions available that just aren't shown in the system prompt context.\n\nI'll first list existing points to understand the current configuration."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2274, "output_tokens": 560, "latency_ms": 11171.421300000475, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "当前处于 CONFIG_HISTORY 阶段，虽然之前无法直接创建点位，但 `enable_history` 可以为标签创建历史配置。让我为这三个 AI 点位启用历史记录：", "reasoning": "The user is now telling me I'm back in CONFIG_HISTORY stage. Looking at the current available tools:\n\n1. manage_history - actions: enable_history, list_history, set_retention\n2. manage_points - actions: list_points\n\nSo in CONFIG_HISTORY stage, I can use `enable_history` to enable history for tags. However, the problem is that the three points (TI-201, PI-201, FI-201) don't exist yet - the previous list showed 0 points.\n\nThe enable_history action might create the config if needed (the description says \"creates the config if needed\"). Let me try to enable history for these three tags. But wait - enabling history doesn't create the point itself, it just enables history sampling for an existing tag.\n\nHowever, looking at the description: \"Turn on historian sampling for a tag (creates the config if needed).\" - it creates the history config, not the tag itself.\n\nI'm in a situation where:\n1. I can't create points (no create_points action available)\n2. I can only enable history for points\n\nLet me try to enable history for the three points anyway - perhaps the system will handle the point creation, or I'll get a clearer error message. I'll try using the default settings since the user didn't specify special parameters.\n\nSince these are AI (analog input) points, I'll use periodic sampling with reasonable defaults. Let me call enable_history for all three tags."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2981, "output_tokens": 530, "latency_ms": 10019.22839999952, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "当前配置遇到了一个前置问题：\n\n**点位 TI-201、PI-201、FI-201 尚不存在**，历史记录配置需要先有点位才能启用。\n\n遗憾的是，在当前可用工具中：\n- `manage_points` 仅支持 **list_points**（查询），不支持创建点位\n- `manage_history` 的 **enable_history** 依赖已存在的点位\n\n---\n\n### 📋 需要您的帮助\n\n要继续完成任务，需要先创建这三个 AI 点位。请选择以下方式之一：\n\n1. **手动创建点位**：在 SCADA 系统中先手动添加 TI-201、PI-201、FI-201（类型：AI），创建完成后告诉我，我再来配置历史记录。\n\n2. **提供点位详细参数**：如果您能提供以下信息，我记录下来供后续配置使用：\n   - 地址/寄存器映射（如 Modbus 地址）\n   - 量程范围（如 0-100%）\n   - 工程单位（如 ℃、kPa、m³/h）\n\n请告诉我您希望如何继续？", "reasoning": "The user is telling me I'm in CONFIG_HISTORY stage again, but the problem remains: the points TI-201, PI-201, FI-201 don't exist yet, so I can't enable history for them. The history configuration requires the points to be created first.\n\nLooking at my available tools:\n1. manage_history - enable_history, list_history, set_retention\n2. manage_points - only list_points\n\nI cannot create points with the current tool set. The `enable_history` action requires existing points (as we saw from the \"POINT_NOT_FOUND\" errors).\n\nAccording to my behavior guidelines: \"若当前阶段的可用工具不满足需求，你可以在回复的纯文本中包含 \"next_state: 阶段名\" 来切换到【可切换的下一阶段】中的合适阶段\"\n\nThe next stages I can switch to are: CONFIG_ALARM, CONFIG_SCRIPT, DEPLOY, DONE, VALIDATE\n\nNone of these seem to help with creating points. The CONFIG_POINT stage was available earlier but it also only had list_points action.\n\nI need to inform the user that the current tool set doesn't support creating new points. The points need to be created before history can be enabled. This is a limitation of the available tools.\n\nLet me be honest with the user about this limitation."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 5, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "HistoryQuery"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 7644, "output_tokens": 1921, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 39290.55260000041}, "judge": null}
