lt_ok": false, "error_code": "ALREADY_EXISTS", "error_msg": "alarm alarm_TI201_HH already exists", "result_data": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 1.4050999998289626, "intended_entities": ["alarms.alarm_TI201_HH"], "referenced_entities": ["points.TI-201"]}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:5c36a73b4c1d2de1572720df5fcdfadf57212e64b3121822dbe294c91f962227", "final_hash": "sha256:af55d165b3ef2bca86c71ae4b9e635a9821c1b293d1a8059ddf10b191dd445f2", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 974, "output_tokens": 316, "latency_ms": 7559.645300000739, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户想为TI-201点位设置HH（高高）和LL（低低）报警，阈值分别为100和10，优先级设为high。\n\n当前阶段是ANALYZE_INTENT，我需要分析用户意图。用户明确要求配置报警，这涉及到报警配置。可用的工具有manage_pages和manage_points，但当前只允许list_pages和list_points操作。这些是查询工具，不能用于创建或修改报警。\n\n配置报警需要访问报警管理工具，但当前阶段没有这类工具。根据行为准则第5条：如果当前阶段的可用工具不满足需求，我可以在回复的纯文本中包含\"next_state: 阶段名\"来切换到合适的阶段。可切换的下一阶段包括：ASK_USER, BIND_POINTS, CONFIG_ALARM, CONFIG_HISTORY, CONFIG_POINT, CONFIG_SCRIPT, DEPLOY, DONE, GENERATE_LAYOUT, MANAGE_PAGES, VALIDATE。\n\n显然，CONFIG_ALARM阶段是用于配置报警的。所以，我应该切换到CONFIG_ALARM阶段。\n\n但首先，我需要确认TI-201点位是否存在。在配置报警之前，最好先验证点位是否存在。我可以先调用manage_points工具来列出点位，查看TI-201是否存在。这有助于了解当前点位状态，并为后续配置提供依据。\n\n让我先调用list_points来查看所有点位。"}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1926, "output_tokens": 289, "latency_ms": 7466.264200000296, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户已切换到CONFIG_ALARM阶段，现在可以使用manage_alarms工具。用户需要为TI-201创建HH（高高）和LL（低低）报警，阈值分别是100和10，优先级设为high。\n\n我需要创建两个模拟量报警。TI-201是模拟量点位（analog），所以应该使用create_analog_alarm动作。每个报警需要唯一的ID，可以分别命名为\"alarm_TI201_HH\"和\"alarm_TI201_LL\"。优先级设为high。HH报警只有高限（high_limit=100），LL报警只有低限（low_limit=10）。默认deadband为0，这样可以。\n\n我需要同时创建两个报警，但工具调用一次只能创建一个。所以需要分两次调用。先创建HH报警，再创建LL报警。\n\n开始创建HH报警："}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2289, "output_tokens": 139, "latency_ms": 3140.6176999998934, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "参数错误，low_limit 不能为 \"None\" 字符串。根据 JSON Schema，low_limit 可以是 number 或 null。我应该设为 null。重新创建 HH 报警："}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2502, "output_tokens": 205, "latency_ms": 4098.331400000461, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要创建两个报警：一个HH（高高）报警，阈值100；一个LL（低低）报警，阈值10。优先级都是high。\n\n对于HH报警，我应该设置high_limit=100，low_limit=null（或不设置）。对于LL报警，设置low_limit=10，high_limit=null。\n\n根据schema，low_limit可以是number或null。我需要用JSON格式的null，而不是字符串\"None\"。\n\n让我重新尝试：先创建HH报警。"}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2781, "output_tokens": 283, "latency_ms": 6003.1659000005675, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户想要为 TI-201 创建两个报警：HH（高高）和 LL（低低）。HH 报警阈值 100，LL 报警阈值 10，优先级都是 high。\n\n我之前尝试创建 HH 报警时遇到了模式错误。问题在于 low_limit 参数。在 JSON 模式中，low_limit 可以是数字或 null。但我传递的是字符串 \"None\"，而不是 JSON null。我需要使用正确的 JSON null 值。\n\n在工具调用中，对于可空参数，我应该传递 null（在 JSON 中是 null），而不是字符串 \"None\"。让我重新尝试。\n\n首先创建 HH 报警：high_limit=100, low_limit=null。然后创建 LL 报警：high_limit=null, low_limit=10。\n\n让我一次创建一个。先创建 HH 报警。"}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3138, "output_tokens": 219, "latency_ms": 5686.735500000395, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要创建两个报警：HH（高高）和LL（低低）。HH报警阈值为100，LL报警阈值为10，优先级都是high。\n\n工具调用时，对于HH报警，low_limit应该为null（或不提供）。对于LL报警，high_limit应该为null。\n\n让我尝试不提供low_limit参数，因为它是可选的。查看schema：low_limit的默认值是null。我可以只提供high_limit=100，不提供low_limit。\n\n同样，对于LL报警，只提供low_limit=10，不提供high_limit。\n\n先创建HH报警："}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3429, "output_tokens": 317, "latency_ms": 7205.590700000357, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要创建两个模拟量报警：一个高高限（HH）报警在100，一个低低限（LL）报警在10。优先级都是high。\n\n让我检查工具的JSON Schema。根据schema，low_limit和high_limit可以是数字或null。我需要确保传递正确的数据类型。\n\n让我尝试不同的方式：不指定low_limit参数（对于HH报警），因为它是可选的（有默认值null）。对于LL报警，不指定high_limit参数。\n\n不过，错误信息说\"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"。这很奇怪，因为我没有指定low_limit。也许系统在内部将其解析为字符串\"None\"？\n\n让我再仔细看错误信息。它说\"unable to parse string as a number\"。也许我需要确保传递的是null而不是字符串\"None\"。在之前的尝试中，我传递了\"None\"作为字符串。实际上，我应该不传递这个参数，或者传递JSON null。\n\n在工具调用中，我应该完全省略不需要的参数。让我再试一次，这次只传递必需的参数和high_limit。"}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3820, "output_tokens": 253, "latency_ms": 5816.29299999986, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要为TI-201点创建两个报警：\n1. HH（高高）报警，阈值100，优先级high\n2. LL（低低）报警，阈值10，优先级high\n\n从之前的尝试来看，我遇到了模式错误。让我仔细看看模式：\n\nlow_limit可以是数字或null。high_limit也可以是数字或null。\n\n我需要传递low_limit为null而不是字符串\"None\"。在JSON中，null应该用None表示，但在工具调用中，我应该传递数字或null。\n\n让我重新尝试，这次使用正确的参数类型。对于HH报警，我应该传递high_limit=100，low_limit=null。对于LL报警，传递high_limit=null，low_limit=10。\n\n让我先尝试HH报警："}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4147, "output_tokens": 264, "latency_ms": 7648.3822999998665, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "根据schema定义，`low_limit`和`high_limit`的默认值为`null`，我可以不传这些参数来使用默认值。让我换一种方式调用：", "reasoning": "The issue is that when I pass `null` for `low_limit`, it seems to be interpreted as a string \"None\" rather than a proper null value. Let me try a different approach - I'll create the alarm without specifying low_limit at all for HH (just don't include it), and for LL without high_limit. Let me look at the schema more carefully.\n\nThe schema says low_limit has `default: null` and `anyOf: [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]`. So null should be valid. But maybe I should simply not include the parameter at all and let it default.\n\nLet me try without including low_limit in the call."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4485, "output_tokens": 382, "latency_ms": 8583.870200000092, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我理解问题了，让我换一种参数传递方式来创建报警。", "reasoning": "I think the issue is that the system is automatically setting low_limit to the string \"None\" when I don't provide it. Let me try providing all parameters explicitly, making sure low_limit and high_limit are proper numbers or null values. \n\nLooking at the schema again:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"},\n```\n\nIt should accept null. But perhaps the JSON serialization is converting my null to string \"None\". Let me try providing the parameters differently.\n\nActually, looking at the error message: \"create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - it seems like low_limit is being passed as a string \"None\" somehow.\n\nLet me try to be very explicit and provide low_limit as an actual number for the LL alarm instead of null.\n\nFor HH alarm (high=100), let me just not include low_limit at all, or try providing both limits explicitly.\n\nWait, I think the issue might be that when I pass `null` or don't include the parameter, the system is converting it to the string \"None\". \n\nLet me try providing low_limit as 0 or some other number to see if that works."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4941, "output_tokens": 490, "latency_ms": 11153.768199999831, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The tool keeps returning the same error about low_limit. Let me try to understand what's happening. It seems like regardless of what I pass for low_limit, it's being interpreted as a string \"None\" rather than a number or null.\n\nLet me look at the schema more carefully:\n```json\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\nIt should accept either a number or null. The error says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" which suggests it's receiving a string \"None\" somewhere.\n\nWait - I think I see the issue. In my XML formatting, I've been passing `None` which in Python would be the string \"None\", not actual null or a number. \n\nLet me try using a proper numeric value for low_limit when I don't want to set it, or try to pass it differently.\n\nActually, looking at the schema again, it says `\"default\": null`. Maybe I should just not include the parameter at all if I want it to be null. But even when I didn't include it, it still failed.\n\nHmm, there might be a bug in the system where low_limit is being set to the string \"None\" by default. Let me try providing an actual number for low_limit. \n\nFor the HH alarm, maybe I should set low_limit to some very low number like -9999 or 0? Or maybe I should try passing low_limit as empty string?\n\nActually wait - let me re-read my parameter values. I see the issue now. In previous calls I was passing `None` as a literal string in the XML. Let me try a different approach - maybe I should just provide a reasonable numeric value for low_limit, or try to omit it entirely in a different way.\n\nLet me try one more time with a proper numeric value for both limits."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5505, "output_tokens": 411, "latency_ms": 8982.542399999147, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The tool schema shows that `low_limit` has `anyOf: [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]` with `default: null`. The error suggests that when I don't include the parameter, it's being passed as a string \"None\" instead of actual null or a number.\n\nLet me try explicitly setting low_limit to a numeric value like -9999 for the HH alarm, or try a different approach. Actually, looking at the schema more carefully:\n\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\nIt should accept null. Let me try passing it as an explicit number instead. For the HH alarm, I'll set low_limit to some extreme low value or just use 0.\n\nActually wait - looking at the error message more carefully: \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - this suggests that somewhere the value is being passed as a string. Maybe the system is converting my parameter to a string \"None\" instead of actual null.\n\nLet me try using actual numeric values for both. For HH alarm, I'll set low_limit to -9999 (or some very low number that won't trigger), and for LL alarm, I'll set high_limit to 9999.\n\nActually, let me just try passing low_limit as a number like 0 or -999 for the HH alarm."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 5, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 39937, "output_tokens": 3568, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 83427.24689999977}, "judge": null}
