}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:5c36a73b4c1d2de1572720df5fcdfadf57212e64b3121822dbe294c91f962227", "final_hash": "sha256:5a1c6f15576a889943a0c28db6202e65f73eaa72e2592bdbcbeb549fe2269fb6", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 974, "output_tokens": 169, "latency_ms": 5553.382799999781, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我来先确认点位 TI-201 是否存在，然后进行报警配置。", "reasoning": "The user wants to set HH (High-High) and LL (Low-Low) alarms for a point called \"TI-201\", with HH alarm at 100, LL alarm at 10, and both with high priority.\n\nFirst, I need to verify that the point \"TI-201\" exists. Let me check the available points using the manage_points tool with list_points action.\n\nThe current workflow is AlarmConfig and the step is discover_points, so discovering what points exist makes sense as a first step.\n\nLet me list the points to verify TI-201 exists."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1779, "output_tokens": 512, "latency_ms": 24062.2543999998, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户明确要求使用当前可用工具继续完成任务，且我已经进入 CONFIG_ALARM 阶段。根据系统提示，当前可用工具是 manage_alarms，支持的 actions 包括 create_digital_alarm, create_analog_alarm, set_threshold, delete_alarm, disable_alarm。\n\n用户的需求是为 TI-201 设置 HH (High-High) 和 LL (Low-Low) 报警，分别在 100 和 10，优先级为 high。TI-201 已确认存在且是模拟量点。因此，我需要使用 create_analog_alarm action 来创建两个模拟量报警：一个用于 HH（高高限），另一个用于 LL（低低限）。\n\n对于 HH 报警：id 可以设为 \"alarm_TI-201_HH\"，tag 为 \"TI-201\"，high_limit 为 100，low_limit 为 null（因为 HH 报警只关心高限），deadband 默认为 0，priority 为 \"high\"。\n\n对于 LL 报警：id 可以设为 \"alarm_TI-201_LL\"，tag 为 \"TI-201\"，high_limit 为 null，low_limit 为 10，deadband 默认为 0，priority 为 \"high\"。\n\n我需要同时创建这两个报警。由于它们之间没有依赖关系，可以并行调用。\n\n现在调用 manage_alarms 工具。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2410, "output_tokens": 264, "latency_ms": 4847.156400000131, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "抱歉，之前的调用参数有误。让我重新创建这两个报警，这次正确设置参数：", "reasoning": "The user wants to create HH and LL alarms for TI-201. The previous attempts failed because I passed \"None\" as a string instead of null. Let me retry with proper null values for the limits that aren't needed.\n\nFor HH alarm: high_limit=100, no low_limit needed\nFor LL alarm: low_limit=10, no high_limit needed\n\nI should not include the parameter at all or use proper null value."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2791, "output_tokens": 406, "latency_ms": 7161.670499999673, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我重新尝试创建这两个报警，这次显式提供 null 值：", "reasoning": "The user wants to create HH and LL alarms for TI-201. The previous attempts failed because the tool is having trouble with the schema validation. Let me try again, this time making sure to provide all required parameters correctly.\n\nLooking at the schema for create_analog_alarm:\n- action: \"create_analog_alarm\" (required)\n- id: string (required)\n- tag: string (required)\n- high_limit: number or null (default null)\n- low_limit: number or null (default null)\n- deadband: number (default 0.0)\n- priority: \"high\", \"medium\", \"low\" (default \"medium\")\n\nFor the HH alarm, I only need high_limit=100, and low_limit should be null (or just not provided).\nFor the LL alarm, I only need low_limit=10, and high_limit should be null (or just not provided).\n\nLet me try providing explicit null values for the unused limits."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3316, "output_tokens": 238, "latency_ms": 4570.742300000347, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我使用正确的 null 值格式来创建这两个报警：", "reasoning": "The issue is that \"None\" is being passed as a string, but the tool expects null for the unused limit parameters. Let me try using null directly without quotes."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3673, "output_tokens": 243, "latency_ms": 4031.042200000229, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试不传递不需要的参数（它们默认为 null）：", "reasoning": "The schema allows null values for high_limit and low_limit. The issue is that \"None\" is being treated as a string. I need to use the JSON null value, not the Python string \"None\". Let me try omitting those parameters entirely since they have default values of null."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4035, "output_tokens": 521, "latency_ms": 9858.210499999586, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试为每个报警同时提供两个限值（用数字值替代 null）：", "reasoning": "Let me try again, but this time I'll set both high_limit and low_limit to numeric values for each alarm:\n\nFor HH alarm: high_limit=100, low_limit=0 (or some arbitrary low value)\nFor LL alarm: high_limit=999 (or some arbitrary high value), low_limit=10\n\nActually, looking at the schema more carefully, it says high_limit and low_limit accept \"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]. The issue might be with how I'm passing null.\n\nLet me try passing both limits as numbers for each alarm:\n- HH alarm: high_limit=100, low_limit=null (but maybe I should just not include it)\n- LL alarm: high_limit=null (but maybe I should just not include it), low_limit=10\n\nWait, looking at the error messages, they're saying \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" for the limit I'm NOT setting. This suggests that when I omit a parameter, it might be getting set to something other than null.\n\nLet me try providing explicit numeric values for both limits in each case:\n- HH alarm: high_limit=100, low_limit=-999 or some very low value\n- LL alarm: high_limit=999 or some very high value, low_limit=10\n\nOr alternatively, let me try providing both limits as numbers that make sense for each alarm type."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4675, "output_tokens": 441, "latency_ms": 8425.288399999772, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试使用 JSON 的 null 值格式：", "reasoning": "This is strange - the tool keeps giving schema errors even when I provide proper numeric values. Let me look at the error messages more carefully:\n\nFor the HH alarm (high_limit=100): \"create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number\"\nFor the LL alarm (low_limit=10): \"create_analog_alarm.high_limit: Input should be a valid number\"\n\nIt seems like when I set high_limit=100, it's erroring on low_limit, and when I set low_limit=10, it's erroring on high_limit. This is very strange behavior.\n\nWait - I just realized something. When I provided low_limit=-9999 and high_limit=9999, it still gave the same errors. That's very strange.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe the issue is with how the JSON is being parsed. Let me try using explicit JSON null notation.\n\nActually, looking at the function call format, maybe I should try using the actual JSON null value. In the parameter block, I can try using `null` without quotes.\n\nLet me try again with explicit null values in JSON format."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5235, "output_tokens": 430, "latency_ms": 8624.406800000543, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我明白了问题所在 - \"None\"被当作字符串处理了。让我直接使用JSON的null值：", "reasoning": "The issue is that when I pass \"None\" as a string for parameters like high_limit or low_limit, it's being treated as a string instead of JSON null. I need to pass actual null values, not the string \"None\".\n\nLooking at the parameter definition again:\n```json\n\"high_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}\n```\n\nThe issue is that I'm passing \"None\" as a string. I need to pass the actual JSON null value. In JSON, null is a special literal, not a string.\n\nLet me try using the actual JSON null value by just not including those parameters at all, or by explicitly passing null (not as a string).\n\nActually, looking at the tool invocation format, I should be able to pass null directly. Let me try that.\n\nWait, I notice the previous attempts all have \