位是否存在。让我用正确的参数再次调用manage_points。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1611, "output_tokens": 85, "latency_ms": 3557.358999999451, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "I see that the type_filter parameter has validation issues. Let me try without the type_filter parameter or with a proper value. Looking at the schema again, it says \"default\": null but the error suggests it needs to be one of the enum values. Let me try without providing the optional parameter."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2743, "output_tokens": 453, "latency_ms": 9630.399399999988, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的，我来按步骤完成泵站画面的配置。首先创建PumpA和PumpB点位，然后创建页面和泵图元。", "reasoning": "The user wants me to create a pump station page with 2 pump widgets bound to PumpA and PumpB points. The current stage is BIND_POINTS, and the available tools are manage_pages, manage_points, manage_graphics, and manage_alarms.\n\nLooking at the tools:\n- manage_pages: Has create_widget and create_page actions\n- manage_points: Has create_point action only\n- manage_graphics: Has apply_flow_layout action\n- manage_alarms: Has create_digital_alarm action\n\nThe user wants to:\n1. Create a pump station page\n2. Add 2 pump widgets\n3. Bind them to PumpA and PumpB points\n\nSince list_points seems to have issues, let me just proceed with the workflow. I need to:\n\n1. First create the PumpA and PumpB points (if they don't exist)\n2. Create the pump station page\n3. Create 2 pump widgets on that page\n\nLet me start by creating the points and the page. The points are likely digital (pump on/off status) or analog (speed, etc.). For a pump, I'll assume they're digital points for simplicity. Let me create them."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3341, "output_tokens": 156, "latency_ms": 3792.6258999996207, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "I need to properly call the tools. Let me check the schemas again:\n\n1. For manage_points with create_point action, I need: action, tag, type (analog/digital/string). I was calling list_points which seems to have a schema issue. Let me just use create_point which is the allowed action in BIND_POINTS stage.\n\n2. For manage_pages with create_page, I need: action, id, name. Optional: resolution, background.\n\nLet me try again with proper parameters."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 5, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "PointBinding"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 10093, "output_tokens": 980, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 27695.792900000015}, "judge": null}
