ith decimal point: 0.0 instead of 0. Or maybe negative infinity? -Infinity? But JSON doesn't support Infinity.\n\nActually, let me check if there's an issue with the tag. The tag exists: PT_COMP_01 is an analog point. That's good.\n\nMaybe I need to set deadband? I've been omitting it, default is 0.0. That should be fine.\n\nLet me try one more time with all parameters explicitly: id, tag, high_limit, low_limit, deadband, priority. All as proper JSON types. If that fails, maybe I should try a different action like set_threshold? But that requires an existing alarm ID.\n\nActually, wait. The tool says \"Currently allowed actions: create_analog_alarm, create_digital_alarm, set_threshold, disable_alarm, enable_alarm\". I've been trying create_analog_alarm. Let me check if maybe I need to use a different action? No, create_analog_alarm is the right one.\n\nMaybe the tool has a bug with null values. Let me try passing low_limit as a very small number instead of null. Like -999999. I already tried that and it failed.\n\nThis is frustrating. The tool keeps giving the same error no matter what I try. Maybe I should ask the user for clarification or suggest an alternative approach? But I'm supposed to be an assistant that completes tasks.\n\nLet me try one more thing: pass all numeric values as strings? But the schema says they're numbers.\n\nActually, let me look at the error message more carefully: \"unable to parse string as a number\". This suggests the tool is receiving a string. But I'm sending numbers. Unless... maybe the tool's implementation has a bug where it's trying to parse the parameter name as a value? Or maybe there's a character encoding issue?\n\nI think I need to try a different approach entirely. Maybe I should use the set_threshold action to create the alarm? No, set_threshold is for updating existing alarms.\n\nWait, maybe I should try creating a digital alarm first to see if that works, then switch to analog? But PT_COMP_01 is analog, not digital.\n\nActually, let me check the manage_alarms tool schema again. It has oneOf with four schemas. I'm using create_analog_alarm schema. Maybe I need to include additional parameters? The schema shows required: [\"id\", \"tag\", \"action\"]. Optional: high_limit, low_limit, deadband, priority.\n\nI'm going to try one more time with minimal parameters: just id, tag, action, and high_limit. Omit low_limit entirely. Let's see if that works."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 8369, "output_tokens": 427, "latency_ms": 10954.526299999998, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我遇到了持续的schema错误。让我重新审视一下工具的参数定义：\n\n```json\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\n这个参数应该接受数字或null。但错误信息说\"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"。这意味着系统收到了一个字符串而不是数字。\n\n让我尝试完全不提供low_limit参数，让系统使用默认值null。根据JSON Schema，如果参数有默认值，应该可以省略它。\n\n但错误仍然出现，即使我省略了low_limit。这可能是一个系统bug。\n\n让我尝试用数字作为low_limit值，比如0或一个很小的数字。但之前尝试0和-999999都失败了。\n\n让我尝试提供一个字符串数字\"0\"？不，这不太可能。\n\n实际上，错误信息说\"unable to parse string as a number\"，这意味着系统期望一个数字，但收到了一个字符串。可能是参数传递的问题。\n\n让我尝试只提供必需的参数：id、tag、action，然后看看会发生什么。如果low_limit有默认值null，应该可以省略。\n\n实际上，我需要再仔细检查一下JSON Schema。在create_analog_alarm的required字段中，只有[\"id\", \"tag\", \"action\"]，所以其他参数都是可选的，有默认值。\n\n但系统仍然尝试解析low_limit。这可能是一个bug。让我尝试传递一个非常具体的数字值，比如1.0或0.0。"}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 5, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 52436, "output_tokens": 5935, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 140035.11939999953}, "judge": null}
{"trace_id": "7d64f74d-767b-43fb-95e9-3adabf3da479", "experiment": {"config_name": "D_hier_rag_workflow", "config_hash": "sha256:17072e90aec915fe54fe88f940444a88d4b03309c40c2be6424c85e6aff05ee6", "code_commit": "6c299a18e517871b834f2a6226522e7c6e6c6e40", "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "dataset_version": "dev", "rep_index": 1, "seed": 43}, "query": {"golden_id": "golden-044", "text": "给不存在的NO_SUCH_TEMP配置高温报警，阈值90", "complexity": "medium", "domain": "alarm"}, "execution": {"started_at": "2026-06-16T05:18:54.850Z", "completed_at": "2026-06-16T05:19:06.610Z", "total_turns": 2, "terminal_state": "CONFIG_ALARM", "early_terminated": false, "termination_reason": null}, "states": [{"name": "ANALYZE_INTENT", "entered_at": "2026-06-16T05:18:54.850Z", "exited_at": "2026-06-16T05:18:59.240Z"}, {"name": "CONFIG_ALARM", "entered_at": "2026-06-16T05:18:59.240Z", "exited_at": "2026-06-16T05:19:06.610Z"}], "tool_calls": [{"turn": 1, "state": "ANALYZE_INTENT", "visible_tools": [{"name": "manage_pages", "allowed_actions": ["list_pages"]}, {"name": "manage_points", "allowed_actions": ["list_points"]}], "visible_count": 2, "selected": "manage_points", "action": "list_points", "args": {"action": "list_points"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"count": 1, "points": [{"tag": "TEMP_REAL", "type": "analog", "unit": "°C", "min": null, "max": null, "description": null}]}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.9030000001075678, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:0d22b095fd587ab7ba4c2964c0315c76dc3f059014e4206987f8ada572f67584", "final_hash": "sha256:0d22b095fd587ab7ba4c2964c0315c76dc3f059014e4206987f8ada572f67584", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 962, "output_tokens": 197, "latency_ms": 4387.222999999722, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我需要先确认系统中是否存在名为 `NO_SUCH_TEMP` 的点位，然后才能为其配置报警。让我先查询一下当前系统中的点位列表。", "reasoning": "The user wants to configure a high temperature alarm for a point called \"NO_SUCH_TEMP\" with a threshold of 90. \n\nAccording to my workflow, I'm in the AlarmConfig workflow, discover_points step. I need to first discover what points exist before configuring alarms.\n\nThe user is asking me to configure an alarm for a point that, based on the name \"NO_SUCH_TEMP\", likely doesn't exist in the system. \n\nLet me first check what points are available in the system using the list_points tool. This will help me verify whether this point exists or not.\n\nI should use the manage_points tool with the list_points action to see all available points."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1794, "output_tokens": 342, "latency_ms": 7366.9095000004745, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "根据系统查询结果，点位 **NO_SUCH_TEMP 不存在**。\n\n当前系统中唯一的点位是：\n| Tag | 类型 | 单位 |\n|------|------|------|\n| TEMP_REAL | analog | °C |\n\n---\n\n**无法为不存在的点位配置报警。** 您有两个选择：\n\n1. **为已存在的 `TEMP_REAL` 配置高温报警（阈值 90）** — 如果这是您想要监控的温度点位\n2. **先创建 `NO_SUCH_TEMP` 点位** — 需要切换到点位配置阶段（BIND_POINTS）来创建该点位，然后再回来配置报警\n\n请问您希望如何处理？", "reasoning": "The user wants to configure a high temperature alarm for a point called \"NO_SUCH_TEMP\" with a threshold of 90. However, I just queried the system and found that this point does NOT exist - the only point in the system is \"TEMP_REAL\".\n\nI'm now in the CONFIG_ALARM phase with only the manage_alarms tool available. I cannot create a new point - I can only create alarms on existing points.\n\nI should inform the user that:\n1. The point \"NO_SUCH_TEMP\" does not exist in the system\n2. The only available point is \"TEMP_REAL\"\n3. Ask if they want to create the alarm on \"TEMP_REAL\" instead, or if they need to first create the \"NO_SUCH_TEMP\" point (which would require going back to the BIND_POINTS or another phase)\n\nI should NOT try to create an alarm on a non-existent point as that would likely fail or cause issues."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 5, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 2756, "output_tokens": 539, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 11759.61610000013}, "judge": null}
